Transfer Factor (TF) values calculated on the major
contaminants indicated individual crop specific uptake
behaviours:

4.6.3 Daily Intake of Metals (DIM)
The highest values were in terms of daily intake of
leafy vegetables and this confirms the claim that the
plant type is a very strong determinant of risk of
exposure. On the whole, the population of territories
surrounding mines is at the highest risk of health
problems, which is also in line with the literature on
food-chain contamination of ASM areas worldwide
(WHO, 2021).

The Pb and Cd levels in the leafy vegetables of Shiroro,
Munya and Rafi were also noted to have a TF 1
pointing to high levels of bioaccumulation.
- Cereals had values of TF low, which was in
agreement with their low efficiency of uptake.
- TF values of root crops (0.40.9) showed translocation
as both soil and tuber.

